course: dictionary
lesson: 1364
title: Canny: clever, careful, or quite good
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Canny has more than one meaning, so the words around it are your clues. In «a canny shopper», canny means clever and careful with money, and hard to trick. A shopper who spots a fake price is canny.
explain: In North East England, people say canny to mean quite, or nice. In «canny good», canny means quite good, not clever good. In «a canny lass», it means a nice girl. Look at the word after canny to choose the meaning.
explain: Always do the swap test: put your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense. In Scotland, «ca' canny» means be careful and go gently, so a Scottish grandad might say it on an icy path.
fact: Canny means clever and careful, especially with money or in business.
fact: A canny person is hard to trick.
fact: In North East England, canny can mean quite or nice: «canny good» means quite good.
fact: In Scotland, «ca' canny» means be careful, go gently.
fact: Canny is an adjective (canny, cannier, canniest). The adverb is cannily.
exercise: «She was a canny shopper, and she spotted the fake price tag.» What does canny mean here? | Very loud and bossy | *Clever and careful, hard to trick | Lost and confused | Tired and slow
exercise: A friend from Newcastle says, «It's canny good!» What does canny mean? | Very sleepy | Lost in the rain | *Quite good | Dangerous and scary
exercise: «The fox was too canny for the hunter.» What does canny suggest about the fox? | It was loud and noisy | *It was hard to trick | It was very hungry | It was lost in the woods
test: «Ca' canny on that icy path,» Grandad says. What does he mean? | Run as fast as you can | Stop and sleep | Dance and sing | *Be careful and go gently
test: The chess player made a canny move that won the game. What does canny mean? | Quiet and slow | Silly and rushed | *Clever and careful | Dirty and unfair
exam: In Newcastle, «it's canny cold» means what? | Lost in the snow | Frozen solid, like ice | *Quite cold | Hard to trick by the cold
